---
import { Upload, FileText, Plus, ArrowUpRight, Users, ShieldCheck } from '@lucide/astro';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import { repositoryUrl, config } from '../data.mjs';
---
<Shell title="Contribute"><section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">CONTRIBUTOR AREA</p><h1>Keep the Playbook Moving.</h1><p>Add the resources your team needs. Contributions use your GitHub permissions and this repository's publishing rules.</p></section><section class="contribution-grid"><article><Upload size={29} /><h2>Upload a Presentation</h2><p>Upload a PPTX or PDF to the presentation folder. Optional metadata can add a summary, audience, and stable title.</p>{repositoryUrl && <a class="button" href={`${repositoryUrl}/upload/main/resources/presentations`} rel="noreferrer">Upload in GitHub<ArrowUpRight size={16} /></a>}<ol><li>Upload the original, distribution-approved file.</li><li>Commit the change to the publishing branch.</li><li>Check the validated build in GitHub Actions.</li></ol><p class="access-notice">{config.publication.mode === 'public-demo' ? 'This is a public demo. Files in its approved presentation folder are downloadable by anyone after publication, including embedded notes and hidden slides.' : 'Every repository reader can inspect committed files and their history, including drafts.'}</p></article><article><FileText size={29} /><h2>Add Structured Guidance</h2><p>Use a resource request form for the title, summary, audience, and source link. Authorized requests become a reviewable pull request; they do not publish on submission.</p>{repositoryUrl && <a class="button button-outline" href={`${repositoryUrl}/issues/new?template=resource.yml`} rel="noreferrer">Open Resource Form<ArrowUpRight size={16} /></a>}<p>Or edit Markdown and its optional metadata directly in the content folder.</p>{repositoryUrl && <a class="text-link" href={`${repositoryUrl}/tree/main/resources`} rel="noreferrer">Browse Content Folders<ArrowUpRight size={16} /></a>}</article><article><Plus size={29} /><h2>Create a New Playbook</h2><p>Start an independent playbook from the clean template. Choose any topic; new instances do not inherit this reference library.</p>{repositoryUrl && <a class="button button-outline" href="https://github.com/elijah286/playbook-template/generate" rel="noreferrer">Use the Clean Template<ArrowUpRight size={16} /></a>}<p class="access-notice">Create it as private. Private website hosting and reader roles require the approved enterprise organization and administrator setup before deployment.</p></article></section></Shell>